// D16851, D16871: a maker with no parameter returns a hole lambda, and its calls' values are
// delivered at two function types. Each call builds its own closure, so the design owes both.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function mk() { return (a) => a + 2.5 }
// @@VALUE@@
mk()
// @@TYPE@@
(a: i32) => f64
// @@PROOF@@
print(v(3))
// @@WANT@@
5.5
// @@VALUE2@@
mk()
// @@TYPE2@@
(a: f64) => f64
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v(0.5))
// @@WANT2@@
3
